 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for delivery.** Browsers receive committed changes via WebSockets connections managed by the server. Preferred over five-second HTTPS polling (introduces multi-second lag and repeated reads) and hosted realtime services (avoids vendor coupling and recurring fees). Requires the store to support replayable change logs, the delivery layer to manage sessions and reconnect logic, and browsers to handle reconnection and catch-up.
